# Code Intelligence knowledge graph cache -- a serialized build artifact
# that bakes in absolute filesystem paths resolved at build time (every
# Model node's filepaths). Committing it lets one machine's absolute paths
# silently overwrite another machine's on checkout -- see todo/contexte.txt
# for the real incident this caused (analyze_security_locks and friends
# returning nothing for every model, on any machine that doesn't match
# whoever last built/committed this file). Always regenerate locally via
# scripts/rebuild_graph.py instead of relying on a committed copy.
# no leading directory -- matches the real file at repo root
# (code_intelligence/graph/loader.py::GRAPH_JSON_PATH resolves to the repo
# root, not code_intelligence/) as well as the orphan stale copy under
# code_intelligence/ (section 2825) -- the old "code_intelligence/
# active_graph.json" pattern never matched the actual tracked file despite
# the comment above explaining exactly why it should be ignored (section
# 869: git check-ignore confirmed 0 matches, 7 commits of an 8.6MB file
# had gone through regardless)

# Generated measurement artefacts: evaluation runs, raw responses, dumps, traces (decision pmm)
captures/

